[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113788,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Salivary carcinosarcoma is characterized by a variable combination of malignant epithelial and sarcomatous tumour components, which may develop from a pre-existent pleomorphic adenoma or de&nbsp;novo.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:03:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113789,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8980/3 Carcinosarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:03:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113790,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B67.Y &amp; XH2W45 Other specified malignant neoplasms of parotid gland &amp; Carcinosarcoma, NOS</p>\r\n<p>2B68.2 &amp; XH2W45 Other specified malignant neoplasms of submandibular or sublingual glands &amp; Carcinosarcoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:03:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113791,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> (true) malignant mixed tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:03:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113792,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:03:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113793,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases of carcinosarcoma manifest in major salivary glands (parotid, 70%; submandibular, 19%); minor gland occurrences are rare {8380049}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:03:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113794,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Carcinosarcomas are typically rapidly growing, large, and infiltrative tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:03:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113795,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "<p >The mean age at presentation is 58&nbsp;years (range: 14&ndash;87&nbsp;years), with no sex predilection {8380049}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T15:48:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113796,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Approximately half of all cases develop from a pre-existent pleomorphic adenoma {3014420; 11197153}. However, it has been shown that some carcinosarcomas arise de&nbsp;novo {2422810; 8380049}. A few cases occurred after radiotherapy {8035132}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:03:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113797,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "<p>A subset of carcinosarcomas harbour <em>PLAG1</em> or <em>HMGA2</em> fusions {36376255}; however, molecular alterations are heterogeneous.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-22T14:28:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113798,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "<p>They are predominantly large, infiltrating tumours (as large as 50&ndash;100&nbsp;mm, mean: 39&nbsp;mm), frequently with necrosis and haemorrhage. A smaller, often sclerotic nodule may represent a pre-existent pleomorphic adenoma.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T15:48:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113799,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The carcinomatous component is most commonly a squamous cell carcinoma or adenocarcinoma, whereas the most common sarcomatous component is a chondrosarcoma {8380049}. The sarcomatous components frequently dominate. Approximately half of the tumours show a pre-existing, often sclerotic pleomorphic adenoma, usually with a carcinomatous (rarely sarcomatous) intracapsular component. Pure intracapsular carcinosarcoma ex pleomorphic adenoma is very rare {2422810}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry is recommended for characterizing the usually heterologous sarcomatous component, and especially for distinguishing carcinosarcoma from other malignancies with high-grade transformation {2422810; 8380049; 22847723}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:03:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113800,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Scattered irregular tissue fragments of large epithelial cells with abundant cytoplasm, large pleomorphic hyperchromatic nuclei, and prominent nucleoli are present, along with occasional giant cells and spindle cells showing atypical nuclei in a background of necrosis. The epithelial component can show squamoid features {29281871}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:03:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113801,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:03:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113802,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> a combined salivary gland tumour with malignant epithelial and mesenchymal components; exclusion of sarcomatoid subtypes of other salivary gland malignancies.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T15:48:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113803,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "<p>Staging follows the eighth edition of the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC)&nbsp;/ American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) TNM staging system.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-09T17:08:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113804,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 354,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis is poor, with a high frequency of local recurrence and lymphatic and haematogenous spread. The largest series showed a mortality rate of 50% and a mean survival time of 3.6&nbsp;years {3014420; 8380049}. Most cases have been reported as case reports with insufficient clinical follow-up {11197153; 17630097; 22847723}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:03:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]